      "extract_protocol_ch1": [
        "PBMC from 20 individuals from ADAPT cohort (10 LC and 10 MC) were genotyped and had PBMCs sequenced using the 10x genomics platform. For each individual, 1 vial (\u223c1mL) of biobanked (frozen) PBMCs was retrieved and thawed. Cell density per vial was roughly 7x106 cells/mL. To this end \u223c30uL was used for single-cell RNA-sequencing, and another fraction (106) for genotyping.",
        "For each batch, single-cell RNA capture and barcoding with the Single Cell 5\u2019 v2.0 NextGEM single cell RNA seq (GEX + VDJ (TCR+BCR) from 10x Genomics, with a target capture of 20,000 cells was performed.",
        "scRNA-seq 5' 10x genomics"
      ],
      "description": [
        "10x Genomics",
        "5_8mths"
      ],
      "data_processing": [
        "The demultiplexing, barcode processing, and gene counting were done with the Cell Ranger software (version 7.0.0). Each pool was processed individually. cellranger mkfastq was run to demultiplex the dual indexed libraries. Config files were setup with expect-cells 20000, and include-introns as TRUE. Mapping and alignment were done to GRCh38 (GEX: refdata-cellranger-GRCh38-2020-A) using STAR within the Cell Ranger suite. The pipeline was executed on a high-performance cluster with a 3.10.0-1160.42.2.el7.x86_64 operating system.",
        "Each sample was SNP genotyped (data not provided as it is protected) and demuxlet was used to demultiplex the pools and assign cells to individuals. The final output from this proccess is provided in the processed files.",
        "Assembly: GRCh38",
        "Supplementary files format and content: Gene expression: tab separated features and barcodes files, and counts in matrix market file format (.mtx).",
        "Supplementary files format and content: Barcode to sample assignment files: tab separated files (combined_results_w_combined_assignments.tsv)"
      ],
